Notes:
  - 'GPU-kernel' isolates the cuSPARSE SpMV call itself (device-resident x/y,
    no PCIe transfer per call) -- the H1-relevant number.
  - 'GPU-rtrip' includes host<->device transfer each call -- the realistic
    cost if this were invoked once per B&B node without keeping x device-
    resident across calls.
  - 'speedup' = CPU time / GPU-kernel time. <1.0x means CPU was faster.
  - These are measurements on this specific RTX 3050 Laptop (4.29GB, 14 SMs),
    not a claim about datacenter-GPU behavior (docs/research/SOTA.md \S0).
